    "  FUN_00594EB0_year_cache_selfcall (B):        4 sampled (~10 real)",
    "  everything else:                             0",
    "So high-volume hooking was NOT the crash cause. Prime suspect:",
    "the INFERRED VA on FUN_0055F080_pyramid_orch — Interceptor.attach",
    "on a wrong address installs a jump patch that crashes as soon as",
    "the CPU reaches that region. Every other Group-A/B hook targets",
    "a confirmed VA and fired zero times during the run.",
    "",
    "Current config: keep everything hooked EXCEPT the inferred",
    "pyramid_orch and the conf_fallback (which shared its VA with",
    "conf_coord — also unverified). If the game survives this run",
    "cleanly, those two are the culprit. If it still crashes, either",
    "another VA is subtly wrong or the crash is unrelated to Frida.",
    "",
    "`va` is the GDI VA. `dd_va_hint` records the DirectDraw",
    "equivalent for cross-reference — the GDI delta is NON-UNIFORM",
    "so it CANNOT be a fixed offset. Every dd_va_hint entry needs a",
    "live confirmation of the corresponding gdi va before enabling.",
    "",
    "Groups C/D/E/F remain disabled — they need GDI resolution first."
